Set errno when find_mount_point() finds no mount point on Windows.
The Windows statfs() returns -1 when find_mount_point() fails, and
"stat -f" then reports errno. When the file existed but no drive or
mounted folder matched it, errno was whatever an earlier call had left
there, so stat printed an unrelated reason, such as "can't read file
system information for 'FILE': Function not implemented". Set errno
to ENODEV in that case.

---
 libbb/find_mount_point.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/libbb/find_mount_point.c
+++ b/libbb/find_mount_point.c
@@ -121,6 +121,8 @@
 		mountEntry = &data->me;
 	}
 	endmntent(mtab_fp);
+	if (!mountEntry)
+		errno = ENODEV; /* for statfs() */
 #endif
 
 	return mountEntry;
